From: SP11 camera <camera@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: simple: per-sensor AWB gain limits and measured fixed gains

The Software ISP white-balance estimator clamps its red and blue gains at
4.0. That ceiling is too low for modules whose own calibration needs more:
the SP11 front IMX681 module's Windows white-balance calibration reaches
8.93x red and 4.28x blue, so the estimator saturates and leaves a green
cast that it cannot remove; the rear module sits just below the same limit.

Add two optional tuning keys:

  Awb:
    maxGains: [red, green, blue]   # estimator ceiling, default 4.0/4.0
    gains:    [red, green, blue]   # fixed measured gains (grey card)

maxGains only raises a ceiling the tuning file states; without the key the
stock 4.0 behaviour is unchanged. gains latches a measured grey-card
correction for every frame and still reports the equivalent colour
temperature so CCM selection keeps working. Both reject non-finite or
out-of-range values so a malformed file fails the IPA instead of silently
distorting colours.

Assisted-by: deepseek-v4.1-flash
